            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1024/1661-8157/a001866</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>COPD is not a homogenous disease but consists of at least four different phenotypes: Emphysema, COPD with chronic bronchitis, asthma-COPD overlap syndrome (ACOS), and COPD with recurrent exacerbations. With differentiation, treatment can be designed phenotype-specific. Some modern drugs are not indicated in all phenotypes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
